  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer can be converted to a voltmeter of full-scale deflection $\\mathrm{V}_{0}$ by connecting a series resistance $\\mathrm{R}_{1}$ and can be converted to an ammeter of full-scale deflection $I_{0}$ by connecting a shunt resistance $\\mathrm{R}_{2}$. What is the current flowing through the galvanometer at its full-scale deflection?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "srjjr",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{0}-\\mathrm{I}_{0} \\mathrm{R}_{2}}{\\mathrm{R}_{1}-\\mathrm{R}_{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LUdWB",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{0}+\\mathrm{I}_{0} \\mathrm{R}_{2}}{\\mathrm{R}_{1}+\\mathrm{R}_{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FwZoh",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{0}-\\mathrm{I}_{0} \\mathrm{R}_{2}}{\\mathrm{R}_{2}-\\mathrm{R}_{1}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "diEfd",
      "text": "$\\frac{V_{0}+l_{0} R_{1}}{R_{1}+R_{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$R_{1}=\\frac{V_{0}}{I_{g}}-G_{\\ldots} \\ldots \\ldots . .(1)$\r\n$\\mathrm{R}_{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{G}}{\\mathrm{I}_{0}-\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{g}}} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots . .(2)$\r\nEliminating G we get\r\n$I_{g}=\\frac{V_{0}-I_{0} R_{2}}{R_{1}-R_{2}}$",
